  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "When possessive adjectives precede a noun, they appear in shortened forms: *mi* (my), *tu* (your), *su* (your/his/her), *nuestro/nuestra* (our) and *su* (your/their). \nThese forms do not change for gender but do change for number. For example, *mi auto* ('my car') and *mis libros* ('my books'). \nUnlike long‑form possessives, shortened forms always appear before the noun."
    }
